<title>IRAN: Iran says its first hovercraft passes tests.</title>
<headline>Iran says its first hovercraft passes tests.</headline>
<dateline>TEHRAN 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iran's first locally-built hovercraft has been successfully tested, a newspaper said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The daily Kayhan said the three-seater Dolphin, designed and built by a military research centre in the southern city of Shiraz, was successfully tested on sea and land.</p>
<p>The $7,000 craft, designed to be used by coastal patrols or for sports, is lighter and faster than an unnamed imported hovercraft of the same size which costs $10,000, the newspaper added.</p>
</text>
